# Shell scripts (git hooks especially) must stay LF regardless of platform
# autocrlf settings — a CRLF-mangled hook can fail silently or behave
# differently across OSes. MCF hit this same class of problem; fixing it
# here from the start rather than as a later cleanup commit.
.husky/* text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# HDF5 files are binary. Without this, a checkout with core.autocrlf=true can rewrite line endings inside a file that git
# mistakes for text, which changes its bytes and its hash (IP-01 T01.14). The committed miniatures in testdata/ are checked by hash.
*.h5 binary

# The hashes of the committed miniatures are read by `sha256sum -c`, which takes a CR at the end of a line as part of the file name: keep this file LF on every platform.
testdata/SHA256SUMS text eol=lf
